(567698, 57218, 14476, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well planned and carefully executed photograph.  It is beautiful.</td>', 'Congratulations on a well planned and carefully executed photograph.  It is beautiful.', '2004-02-04 00:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(567705, 57203, 14476, '<td valign="top">Congratulations.  Beautifully done!  Hope you had a nice dinner later.</td>', 'Congratulations.  Beautifully done!  Hope you had a nice dinner later.', '2004-02-04 00:51:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(567792, 57218, 13669, '<td valign="top">Hot Dog I guessed right!!! Excellent photo, and thank you for sharing!</td>', 'Hot Dog I guessed right!!! Excellent photo, and thank you for sharing!', '2004-02-04 01:23:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(567795, 57297, 13136, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who gave me high votes and I apologize to those who gave 1''s and 2''s.<br/> <br/>Yes, this was definitly a setup shot. It started out as just a water carrier, then when I thought about the title, my love for music led me to the Fifth Dimension song ''Aquarius! Let The Sunshine In''. That meant that the sun had to shine in through the water bottle. That still wasn''t enough for me. My sick sense of humor came through and said ''When you have the sun, you have to have the moon''.<br/> <br/>Thanks to all who restored my faith in the general sense of humor on this site. I will continue to try to bring a smirk to everyone''s face.<br/> <br/>P.S. I refuse to reveal who''s butt crack that is (but I do own a remote).</td>', 'Thanks to all who gave me high votes and I apologize to those who gave 1''s and 2''s. Yes, this was definitly a setup shot. It started out as just a water carrier, then when I thought about the title, my love for music led me to the Fifth Dimension song ''Aquarius! Let The Sunshine In''. That meant that the sun had to shine in through the water bottle. That still wasn''t enough for me. My sick sense of humor came through and said ''When you have the sun, you have to have the moon''. Thanks to all who restored my faith in the general sense of humor on this site. I will continue to try to bring a smirk to everyone''s face. P.S. I refuse to reveal who''s butt crack that is (but I do own a remote).', '2004-02-04 01:27:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(567796, 56709, 14863, '<td valign="top">Well, okay, there''s what this is ''cause everyone seems a little confused. There''s a river running by my school''s library. This photo is a rock and plant and the water running. I didn''t do  anything to it, this is the way it came  out in  the camera.</td>', 'Well, okay, there''s what this is ''cause everyone seems a little confused. There''s a river running by my school''s library. This photo is a rock and plant and the water running. I didn''t do  anything to it, this is the way it came  out in  the camera.', '2004-02-04 01:28:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(567830, 57217, 16363, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, I agree with the lightings comments, it is harsh. I wasn''t very satisfied myself but wanted to submit my first pic altough I didn''t have much time to make something :-)</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, I agree with the lightings comments, it is harsh. I wasn''t very satisfied myself but wanted to submit my first pic altough I didn''t have much time to make something :-)', '2004-02-04 01:46:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(567831, 56780, 4258, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for my highest till date score despite the obvious goof-up with the backdrop. Those of you who said they wanted to see more of the model - the intention of the picture was to evoke that that tantalising appeal... and want for more...</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for my highest till date score despite the obvious goof-up with the backdrop. Those of you who said they wanted to see more of the model - the intention of the picture was to evoke that that tantalising appeal... and want for more...', '2004-02-04 01:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(567835, 57159, 13669, '<td valign="top">I''d like to say thanks to all those who voted for me, in either direction.  This was my first submission, and I thought it worked out quite well.  Thanks again, and this won''t be the last time you will see me.</td>', 'I''d like to say thanks to all those who voted for me, in either direction.  This was my first submission, and I thought it worked out quite well.  Thanks again, and this won''t be the last time you will see me.', '2004-02-04 01:50:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(567850, 57218, 12151, '<td valign="top">This is really great- I''d even think about *not* spot-editing those two screws in the wall.  The more I look at it, the more I want to accomodate the screws into the image since it looks so enticing.  They''re like the moon and stars.</td>', 'This is really great- I''d even think about *not* spot-editing those two screws in the wall.  The more I look at it, the more I want to accomodate the screws into the image since it looks so enticing.  They''re like the moon and stars.', '2004-02-04 02:01:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(567853, 56780, 9073, '<td valign="top">Tarique, <br/> <br/>You deserved and got a good score with this entry. You clearly met the challenge. The set up was effective, even a touch sexy. There''s a lovely softness on the model and the hint of nudity with drapery really lends itself to an ancient Greek theme. <br/> <br/>Did you notice a rather strange top left corner? No, I''m sure you didn''t.</td>', 'Tarique,  You deserved and got a good score with this entry. You clearly met the challenge. The set up was effective, even a touch sexy. There''s a lovely softness on the model and the hint of nudity with drapery really lends itself to an ancient Greek theme.  Did you notice a rather strange top left corner? No, I''m sure you didn''t.', '2004-02-04 02:04:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(567872, 57203, 12160, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the comments. I truly wasn''t thinking of a ribbon here, but I accept it. :) Had fun doing it but didn''t get to eat it!</td>', 'Thanks everyone for the comments. I truly wasn''t thinking of a ribbon here, but I accept it. :) Had fun doing it but didn''t get to eat it!', '2004-02-04 02:19:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(567891, 56709, 3942, '<td valign="top">Hi Liz, <br/> <br/>congrats again on this shot. The more I look at it, the more I like it. This is a highly impressive shot to me, thanks for sharing!</td>', 'Hi Liz,  congrats again on this shot. The more I look at it, the more I like it. This is a highly impressive shot to me, thanks for sharing!', '2004-02-04 02:59:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(567892, 57218, 12425, '<td valign="top">Great shot, this jumped out at me immediately, well deserved!</td>', 'Great shot, this jumped out at me immediately, well deserved!', '2004-02-04 03:08:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(567893, 57218, 3942, '<td valign="top">Thank you!! <br/> <br/>Im very proud of this, because I got the last blue ribbon only by a cheap trick ;-). If there are any questions left after reading the photo details, please feel free to ask me...<br/> <br/>Regarding to your comments: Yes, you are right, this shot is techically not as perfect as it could have been. Susi is a little bit out of focus, because of the long time exposure. A flashlight probably would have minimized the blurred parts of this shot. But in this special case I prefer the warm and softer touch of a diffuse lighting by a lamp. If you want to have a look at a spot-edited version without the two distracting dots in the background, please visit my homepage.<br/> <br/>Special thanks to my GF Susi for her incredible patience and for setting my heart on fire! By the way: Her zodiac sign is Leo, but this was much too difficult to paint with a bike-lamp... :-)<br/></td>', 'Thank you!!  Im very proud of this, because I got the last blue ribbon only by a cheap trick ;-). If there are any questions left after reading the photo details, please feel free to ask me... Regarding to your comments: Yes, you are right, this shot is techically not as perfect as it could have been. Susi is a little bit out of focus, because of the long time exposure. A flashlight probably would have minimized the blurred parts of this shot. But in this special case I prefer the warm and softer touch of a diffuse lighting by a lamp. If you want to have a look at a spot-edited version without the two distracting dots in the background, please visit my homepage. Special thanks to my GF Susi for her incredible patience and for setting my heart on fire! By the way: Her zodiac sign is Leo, but this was much too difficult to paint with a bike-lamp... :-)', '2004-02-04 03:08:33.000000', NULL, 0),
