(568206, 57203, 6624, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on an image that fit the challenge and was powerful as well</td>', 'Congratulations on an image that fit the challenge and was powerful as well', '2004-02-04 10:06:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(568262, 56784, 12095, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dmjbtpc:</b></div><hr/><i> I''d like to know how this was done.  Was it two flashguns between crab and poster (one at crab, one at poster)?  nicely done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>TV flat on the ground with a picture of the moon, pexiglass on top of the TV with a space in between. A small Wallmart clip on desk light placed between the tv &amp; pexiglass, Crab on top!  The cord for the desk light exits where the crabs back touches the edge of the moon.  Since the cord is black you cannot see the cord for the light.<br/> <br/>The reflection is because I didn''t get the camera peferectly above the TV/crab. It was at a slight angle and that caused the reflection. I setup and took the picture early Sunday morning, thought about re-taking it to get rid of the reflection but was out of time....Wife and baby were up already....time to go to church!<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the comments!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-04 10:48:06.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by dmjbtpc: I''d like to know how this was done.  Was it two flashguns between crab and poster (one at crab, one at poster)?  nicely done.   TV flat on the ground with a picture of the moon, pexiglass on top of the TV with a space in between. A small Wallmart clip on desk light placed between the tv & pexiglass, Crab on top!  The cord for the desk light exits where the crabs back touches the edge of the moon.  Since the cord is black you cannot see the cord for the light. The reflection is because I didn''t get the camera peferectly above the TV/crab. It was at a slight angle and that caused the reflection. I setup and took the picture early Sunday morning, thought about re-taking it to get rid of the reflection but was out of time....Wife and baby were up already....time to go to church! Thanks for all the comments!', '2004-02-04 10:43:02.000000', '2004-02-04 10:48:06.000000', 0),
