(572224, 57299, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, I think the elements that help to make your photo are the bird and the lighting.  The photo does seem to tilt, not sure if the horizon is actually crooked or if seems so because of the sand in the lower left to lower right edge.  I believe cropping this section out, tho leaving the bird a little tight would serve to create a 1/3 2/3 image a bit more.  It may also help the viewer not to want to tilt head so much to look at it.  The bird the sun add a nice balance to the shot, they create a good tension.  If the shutter speed was a little faster it may have helped to get a bit sharper waves.  Overall a nice sunset shot.  <br/>Well done and happy shooting!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, I think the elements that help to make your photo are the bird and the lighting.  The photo does seem to tilt, not sure if the horizon is actually crooked or if seems so because of the sand in the lower left to lower right edge.  I believe cropping this section out, tho leaving the bird a little tight would serve to create a 1/3 2/3 image a bit more.  It may also help the viewer not to want to tilt head so much to look at it.  The bird the sun add a nice balance to the shot, they create a good tension.  If the shutter speed was a little faster it may have helped to get a bit sharper waves.  Overall a nice sunset shot.  Well done and happy shooting!', '2004-02-07 22:54:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(572505, 57188, 13403, '<td valign="top">yeah, aries!</td>', 'yeah, aries!', '2004-02-08 14:00:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(572570, 56815, 7889, '<td valign="top">Maybe its not to clear in the photo but the larger fish had attempted to eat a smaller fish and it was stuck in its mouth and caused his death. This was taken as it floated down the Kennet and Avon Canal. I had to up the ISO to 1600 to get this so there is some noise present.<br/>Thanks for the comments, especially yours John they are appreciated.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-08 15:37:54.</i></td>', 'Maybe its not to clear in the photo but the larger fish had attempted to eat a smaller fish and it was stuck in its mouth and caused his death. This was taken as it floated down the Kennet and Avon Canal. I had to up the ISO to 1600 to get this so there is some noise present.Thanks for the comments, especially yours John they are appreciated.', '2004-02-08 15:37:23.000000', '2004-02-08 15:37:54.000000', 0),
(573406, 57257, 14773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Mundi:</b></div><hr/><i> no its me!! im just very pretty </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And humble apparently!</td>', 'Originally posted by Mundi: no its me!! im just very pretty   And humble apparently!', '2004-02-09 12:34:20.000000', NULL, 0),
